      "content": "thanks for that. one thing that's been a real headache for our audit team is verifying the absolute thoroughness of the deletion. we keep running into these weird little \"pockets\" of data in unindexed logs or old archives that seem to just vanish from our standard reporting tools when we try to scan them. how do we actually go about tracking down these hidden remnants to make sure nothing is being left behind in the cracks?",
